OL,3,GNEWSAPub faces cut-off threat over #55k
OL,4,Aelectric bill
OL,5,
OL,6,FA pub is facing the threat of having
OL,7,Fits electricity cut off over a disputed
OL,8,Fbill of more than #55,000, despite
OL,9,Fclaims the meter is faulty.
OL,11,FBecky Gomery and Rich Spicer, who own
OL,12,Fthe Chequers Inn in Lamberhurst, Kent,
OL,13,Fare disputing the amount with Yorkshire
OL,14,FGas and Power (YGP) after they were
OL,15,Fbilled #55,589.77 and warned that
OL,16,Ffailure to respond could lead to
OL,17,Fdisconnection.
OL,19,FThe energy ombudsman has said YGP
OL,20,Fshould investigate concerns about the
OL,21,Fmeter and look at whether the pub had
OL,22,Fbeen billed accurately.
OL,23,APub: 07-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,322,320,200,140,0,100
